Z||000000||jlruiz67||07-16-2000||07:31 AM||||"Custom modified front hubs for all 84-87 Fiero's. They enable you to install the larger Grand Am rotors and calipers. This piece is a direct replacement for your old front rotor, because that is what it once was. It is a Fiero rotor that has been machined down to a hub for the Grand Am rotor. With these hubs the process becaomes an esy bolt on job." <P>Now this is only the hubs, I still have to buy rotors, calipers and pads. The price for the hubs is $80.00, What do you think? is it worth it? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||07-16-2000||07:59 AM||||You can get your own rotors turned down for probably $40 to $60, but since they are charging for the cores and this is the price outright, then it's probably a fair price. If you shop around though, you might find a better deal. Hopefully, it's quality work.||||reg||1
